Hi beautiful people!
Here we are from the [b]Pride Run Radio[/b]! 
(yes, it is only a post, not a podcast. But we like it to call it 'Radio'!)

As told in the title (and in the subtitle, and in the brief description), we are near the release!!!
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/32922079/dee6f10c9e2490e58a8840bd5b81b94f0346dbe8.gif[/img]

We can say that the version 1.0 is ALMOST finished :)

[b]Giacomo[/b] the art director, [b]Ilaria[/b] and [b]Elena[/b] are working to additional animated supercool videosequence for the game ending cut scene; 

[b]Mauro[/b] the musician is postproducing the Hard Ton soundtrack and Max the singer is warming his voice for the last minute choruses; 

[b]Ivan[/b] the game director talks continuously at the phone while writing emails while drawing additional pixel-art for some OMG-we-forgot-this-icon-for-that-feedback; 

[b]Massimo[/b] the producer is doing 23353 things in the same time; 
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/32922079/eba8a320d4566335e1f107dec02ed1c84f4fa0ef.png[/img]
[b]Davide[/b] the programmer is writing code with 12 fingers;  

testers [b]Kyle[/b] and [b]Simone[/b] are playing 24hours per day and balancing data structures; 

[b]Marianna[/b] is normalizing the last audio effects;

[b]Daniele[/b] is finishing last objects for the London Scenario;
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/32922079/64580203e9c6b78e4cae7a3f1f4d0940c267cf22.png[/img]

[b]Alessia[/b] just finished Johannesburg (2 weeks ago, to say the truth)
[b]Maria Luisa[/b] is already working (and almost finishing) the Sao Paulo scenario, which will be added in one next update;

[b]Marco[/b] is working on the release trailer;

...everyone who pass in our office is [i]gently[/i] forced to play Pride Run, to have as much feedbacks as possible! Hunting & mashing bugs, refining graphics and parameters, balancing audio levels here and there... and adding some we-absolutely-have-to-add-this-feature-NOW!
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/32922079/acc970adea99b66a6b339b74d883748cf09146f1.png[/img]
On the other side of Europe (at least for now! If Boris won't create more trouble) in London our colleagues of [b]Green Man Gaming[/b] are preparing store assets, managing last localizations, starting some external QA process, signing last agreements... and preparing to party in the GaymingMag.com event in Soho!

RUN PRIDE RUN!!!
